# Code metrics (file size + complexity)

Shared limits: `scripts/code-metrics-limits.cjs`. Enforced in **two places** with the same thresholds:

| Metric | Warn | Error (hard) |
|--------|------|--------------|
| File lines (blank lines + `//`/`/*` comments skipped) | 400 | 800 |
| Cyclomatic complexity per function | 15 | 25 |

## ESLint (IDE + `npm run lint`)

| Rule | Severity |
|------|----------|
| `max-lines` | warn @ 400 |
| `local/max-lines-strict` | error @ 800 |
| `complexity` | warn @ 15 |
| `local/complexity-strict` | error @ 25 |

## Typecheck (`tsc` + metrics script)

`npm run typecheck` = `tsc --noEmit` **then** `scripts/check-code-metrics.mjs` (TypeScript AST, same limits).

Standalone: `npm run qualitygate:metrics`

Pre-commit runs metrics on **staged** files only (`scripts/pre-commit-typecheck.mjs`).

## Agent workflow

**After editing any `src/**/*.ts(x)` file:**

```bash
npm run qualitygate:file -- src/path/to/File.tsx   # TSC + ESLint + code metrics (~5–15s)
```

**Many failures?** `npm run qualitygate:capture` once → fix one item at a time from `.local/quality-backlog.md` → rescan every **5** fixes. See `quality-backlog.mdc`.

**Every 3 completed todos:** `npm run qualitygate:changed`

**Do not** `eslint-disable` these rules. **Do not** use bulk `node -e` / heredoc scripts to rewrite `src/` — extract incrementally (see `refactor-discipline.mdc`).

## Splitting oversized files

1. Plan targets first (layout → hooks → panels → utils).
2. **One extract per step** — move one unit, fix imports, delete from source.
3. Gate with `qualitygate:file` before the next extract.
4. New files should land **≤400 lines**; **800 is a hard error**.

Route pages (`src/app/**/page.tsx`) stay thin shells — orchestration belongs in `src/domains/<module>/`.

## Legacy debt

Full-repo `npm run typecheck` / `qualitygate:metrics` may fail on pre-existing violations. **Touched files must be clean** before handoff. Tracker: `SRC-QUALITY-TRACKER.md` · refresh: `npm run qualitygate:tracker -- --skip-tsc`.

## Exempt from metrics rules

`eslint.config.js`, `eslint-rules/**`, `scripts/**` (tooling only — not `src/`).
